["Plan: 'pure summarize() maps a list-jobs payload ... to one line per non-successful job'","gerrit-verify.yaml vote job runs the summarize step in-process, so /jobs includes vote itself with a null/in_progress conclusion","The plan enumerates statuses as 'failure/cancelled/timed_out' but does not state how a job with no conclusion (in_progress) is treated"],"finding":"The summarize step reads the current run's /jobs list while the vote job is itself running, but the plan does not specify that summarize() excludes still-running jobs (which have no conclusion yet), risking the vote job listing itself as a non-successful job.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f55b6f84ac2a07d5d","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 and step 2 (jobs gathered via gh api runs/<id>/jobs)","norm_id":"n01735954f4de6b24","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["Every -1 run: the vote job is in_progress when it queries its own run's jobs; if a null conclusion is treated as non-successful, the triage comment lists the vote job itself as a spurious failure line"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"State that summarize() filters to jobs whose conclusion is in {failure, cancelled} (mapping the annotation to timed_out) and drops any job whose conclusion is null/empty (queued/in_progress), and add a test feeding a payload that includes the running vote job to assert it is omitted.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm (against GitHub REST docs, not memory) that the id returned by `actions/runs/<id>/jobs` is directly usable as the check-run id in `check-runs/<id>/annotations`, and record the citation in the plan; if the ids differ, name the correct linkage (e.g. via the job's check_run reference) before committing.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'a job id IS its check-run id'","AC1 depends on the annotation ('exceeded the maximum execution time') to render TIMED OUT; AC10 asserts per-job annotations fetched from 'check-runs/<id>/annotations'","Plan also states the best-effort degrade: 'a failed read degrades wording but must not fail the step' — so a wrong id fails silently rather than loudly","EVIDENCE CLASS: Partially-verified — the two endpoints exist and are on an already-used vendor (GitHub REST), but the cross-endpoint id-equivalence surface is unconfirmed from the plan and could not be probed via repo tools"],"finding":"The annotation-fetch path depends on the asserted identity 'a job id IS its check-run id' to address check-runs/<job id>/annotations, but the plan asserts this without verifying it against GitHub API docs; if the id returned by actions/runs/<id>/jobs is not usable as a check-run id, the annotation read 404s and every timed-out job silently degrades to cancelled-without-annotation — the very indistinguishability the plan exists to remove.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f33b95b4731b6554f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location